            <ArticleTitle>Vesicoscopic ureteral reimplant: is there a role in the age of robotics?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>53-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.ucl.2014.09.005</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0094-0143(14)00101-3</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Vesicoscopic ureteral reimplantation is a challenging procedure to learn but does have outcomes equivalent to standard open repair. Children objectively have less pain than after an open cross-trigonal repair. Operative times compare favorably to other forms of minimally invasive surgery.</AbstractText>
